@idea
Feature: bira idea

  Background:
    Given I run "bira init --name test-project"

  Scenario: Idea add creates an idea
    When I run "bira idea add my-idea"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "Created idea"
    And output contains "my-idea"

  @json
  Scenario: Idea add --json returns structured output
    When I run "bira idea add json-idea --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output as JSON at path "$.title" equals "json-idea"
    And output as JSON at path "$.status" equals "inbox"

  @json
  Scenario: Idea add with --desc sets description
    When I run "bira idea add described --desc 'an interesting concept' --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output as JSON at path "$.description" equals "an interesting concept"

  @json @tags
  Scenario: Idea add with --tags
    When I run "bira idea add tagged --tags 'ux,perf' --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output as JSON at path "$.tags" exists

  @list
  Scenario: Idea list shows ideas
    Given I run "bira idea add list-me"
    When I run "bira idea list"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "list-me"

  @json @list
  Scenario: Idea list --json returns array
    Given I run "bira idea add listed"
    When I run "bira idea list --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "listed"

  @list
  Scenario: Idea list --status filters by status
    Given I run "bira idea add inbox-idea"
    When I run "bira idea list --status inbox"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "inbox-idea"

  @failure @list
  Scenario: Idea list --status with invalid value fails
    When I run "bira idea list --status nosuchstatus"
    Then exit code is not 0
    And stderr contains "invalid status"

  @show
  Scenario: Idea show displays idea details
    Given I run "bira idea add show-me --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $IID
    When I run "bira idea show $IID"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "show-me"
    And output contains "ID:"
    And output contains "Status:"

  @json @show
  Scenario: Idea show --json returns structured output
    Given I run "bira idea add show-json --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $IID
    When I run "bira idea show $IID --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output as JSON at path "$.title" equals "show-json"
    And output as JSON at path "$.status" equals "inbox"

  @failure @show
  Scenario: Idea show unknown ID returns exit 2
    When I run "bira idea show deadbeef"
    Then exit code is 2

  @json @triage
  Scenario: Idea triage sets priority and moves to triaged
    Given I run "bira idea add to-triage --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $IID
    When I run "bira idea triage $IID --priority high --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output as JSON at path "$.status" equals "triaged"
    And output as JSON at path "$.priority" equals "high"

  @triage
  Scenario: Idea triage human output confirms triage
    Given I run "bira idea add triage-human --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $IID
    When I run "bira idea triage $IID --priority medium"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "Triaged idea"

  @json @promote
  Scenario: Idea promote creates a feature
    Given I run "bira idea add to-promote --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $IID
    When I run "bira idea promote $IID --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output as JSON at path "$.title" equals "to-promote"
    And output as JSON at path "$.status" equals "proposed"
    And output as JSON at path "$.promoted_from" exists

  @promote
  Scenario: Idea promote human output confirms promotion
    Given I run "bira idea add promote-human --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $IID
    When I run "bira idea promote $IID"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "Promoted idea"

  @note
  Scenario: Idea note appends a note
    Given I run "bira idea add to-note --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $IID
    When I run "bira idea note $IID 'remember this'"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "Note added to idea"

  @delete
  Scenario: Idea delete removes the idea
    Given I run "bira idea add to-delete --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $IID
    When I run "bira idea delete $IID"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "Deleted idea"

  @delete @failure
  Scenario: Idea delete unknown ID returns exit 2
    When I run "bira idea delete deadbeef"
    Then exit code is 2
